// Hosted FactLot: api.factlot.com (MCP, REST, OpenAPI, billing) and the landing page.
// Deploy: npm run deploy:cloudflare (from the repo root). Secrets (set by a maintainer, never in
// this file): STRIPE_SECRET_KEY (required for billing; checkout opens only with a live key),
// STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET (recommended: plan changes, refunds and disputes apply at once),
// IP_HASH_SALT (a long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; salts the hash that names a
// keyless caller's meter, so stored names cannot be traced back to an address. Set it once with
// `npx wrangler@4 secret put IP_HASH_SALT`; changing it restarts that day's free counts).
// RECOVERY_SIGNING_SECRET (a long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; signs the
// lost-key recovery links and the OAuth "Email me a sign-in link" option. Without it, and
// without the EMAIL binding below, /account says email recovery is being set up and the OAuth
// sign-in page offers the key and the free tier only).
// ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (optional; an API key from FactLot's commercial Anthropic organization, set
// with `npx wrangler@4 secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). It turns on the two model-backed tools,
// doc_extract_lease and report_narrative (Pro and Team only). Without it they are not listed and
// their routes answer 503 ModelUnavailable, so deploying before it is set is safe; every other
// tool runs without a model either way. Delete the secret to turn them off again.
// GATING_ENABLED (a variable in `vars` below, "true": paid gating is on). Keyless and free-OAuth
// callers then get registry_get, and the subject of registry_tx_equity_candidates, with the
// current roll year's values only (value_history, history) and registry batch tools answer PlanRequired; Pro and Team keep everything, and
// checkout accepts ?plan=pro&interval=year (price factlot_pro_yearly_v1). Any value other than
// "true", or removing the variable, turns gating off again.
// FREE_KEY_ENABLED (a variable in `vars` below, "true": the free API key by email is on).
// Needs the EMAIL binding and RECOVERY_SIGNING_SECRET below. Unset or any other value: POST
// /v1/keys/free and /account/free-key answer 404 and /account shows no form; keys already issued
// keep working. Publish the privacy notice and terms that describe it before setting it.
// WATCH_LISTS_ENABLED (a variable, "true": watch lists are on; see README.md). Unset here, so the
// watch_* tools are unlisted, /v1/watch/* answers 404 and no check runs. Turning it on needs no
// new binding (storage is the LIMITER class and KV); deploy the registry Worker first (its
// /get-many route lets one call read 50 subjects). Alert emails also need a cron trigger (the
// commented "triggers" below), the EMAIL binding and RECOVERY_SIGNING_SECRET; the alert emails
// print POSTAL_ADDRESS (below) at their foot when it is set and are sent without it.
//
// LIFECYCLE_EMAILS_ENABLED ("true": the lifecycle emails are on; deliberately NOT set in `vars`
// below). Needs FREE_KEY_ENABLED's bindings, the secret POSTAL_ADDRESS (one line, printed in the
// footer of every optional note; without it none is sent) and, for the time-based notes, a cron
// trigger (the commented "triggers" below; none is configured). Unset or any
// other value: no lifecycle message is sent, the consent boxes are not shown, /account/stop and
// /account/lifecycle answer 404 and the checkout return link is ignored. See src/lifecycle.ts.
//
// OAuth 2.1 for header-less MCP clients (src/oauth.ts) needs no new binding: its records live in
// the KEYS namespace under the `oauth:` prefix. It does need `global_fetch_strictly_public`
// below, which lets the authorization server verify Client ID Metadata Documents (ChatGPT's
// client id is one) without same-zone origin routing. The flag only concerns global fetch();
// this Worker reaches its own services through bindings (REGISTRY, ASSETS, the Node handler).
{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "factlot-api",
  "main": "src/worker.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-01",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat", "global_fetch_strictly_public"],
  // Unminified: the minified bundle failed at module start (zod schemas via the MCP SDK). With the
  // report engine (pdf-lib) and pdf.js (unpdf) the upload is near 8 MB (about 1.9 MB gzipped).
  "minify": false,
  // Reports and the model-backed tools build files and read PDFs in the Worker, which takes more
  // than the free plan's 10 ms of CPU per request. The account is on the Workers Paid plan, so the
  // limit is raised and reports are open (REPORTS_ENABLED in vars). On a free-plan deployment
  // remove the limits block and the var: reports then answer 503 ReportsUnavailable.
  "limits": { "cpu_ms": 30000 },
  "workers_dev": false,
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "api.factlot.com", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "factlot.com", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "www.factlot.com", "custom_domain": true },
  ],
  // USAGE_COUNTERS_ENABLED "true": the usage counters are on (src/usage.ts, README.md in this
  // folder); remove it to turn them off. The privacy notice describes them.
  // PROPERTY_PAGES_ENABLED "true": the public property pages and their sitemaps are on
  // (src/property-pages.ts). A parcel gets a page when every source behind a shown fact records
  // redistribution as permitted or attribution_required, or is listed in
  // PROPERTY_PAGES_EXTRA_SOURCES (comma-separated source ids). The Texas appraisal districts record
  // "unknown" and are listed here by the operator's decision of 2026-11-12. Not listed: Tarrant
  // (withheld from every hosted tool), Ector (its site footer reserves all rights), and Brazos,
  // Galveston, Guadalupe, Jefferson, Kaufman and Nueces until their ownership links are rebuilt
  // (prior roll years' links still read as current there). Remove a source id, or the variable, and redeploy to take its
  // pages down; set PROPERTY_PAGES_ENABLED to anything else to turn every page off.
  "vars": {
    "SITE_URL": "https://factlot.com",
    "API_URL": "https://api.factlot.com",
    "REPORTS_ENABLED": "true",
    "USAGE_COUNTERS_ENABLED": "true",
    "GATING_ENABLED": "true",
    "FREE_KEY_ENABLED": "true",
    "PROPERTY_PAGES_ENABLED": "true",
    "PROPERTY_PAGES_EXTRA_SOURCES": "tx-harris-cad,tx-harris-cad-buildings,tx-dallas-cad,tx-travis-cad,tx-collin-cad,tx-denton-cad,tx-williamson-cad,tx-cameron-cad,tx-grayson-cad,tx-midland-cad",
  },
  // KEYS also holds the OAuth server's records (clients, grants, hashed tokens) under the `oauth:`
  // prefix (src/oauth.ts), so OAuth needs no binding of its own.
  "kv_namespaces": [
    { "binding": "KEYS", "id": "c49c4b0d0bd94c52b1d2d474ad499fcb" },
  ],
  // Registry tools answer from the factlot-registry Worker (deploy/registry), reachable only
  // through this binding. Deploy it first: npm run deploy:registry -- <pack dir>.
  "services": [{ "binding": "REGISTRY", "service": "factlot-registry" }],
  // LIMITER: per-minute limits (memory), registry lookup quotas and checkout-session claims
  // (SQLite storage of the same class; no new migration needed).
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [{ "name": "LIMITER", "class_name": "RateLimiterObject" }],
  },
  "migrations": [{ "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["RateLimiterObject"] }],
  // Cron triggers (examples only; none is configured). The scheduled handler (src/worker.ts)
  // dispatches on the cron string: "*/15 * * * *" runs the watch-list check (src/watch-check.ts,
  // WATCH_LISTS_ENABLED; a run with no new pack is one registry and one Durable Object request),
  // "0 15 * * *" the lifecycle sweep (src/lifecycle.ts, LIFECYCLE_EMAILS_ENABLED). Uncomment the
  // line for each feature you turn on; each job does nothing while its variable is off.
  // "triggers": { "crons": ["*/15 * * * *", "0 15 * * *"] },
  // Email (welcome email after purchase, lost-key recovery links), through Cloudflare Email
  // Service: factlot.com is onboarded for Email Sending (Compute > Email Service > Email Sending;
  // the cf-bounce MX, SPF, DKIM and _dmarc records are managed there) and RECOVERY_SIGNING_SECRET
  // is set. Sending from accounts@factlot.com needs the Workers Paid plan. Without this binding
  // the Worker skips the welcome email and /account says recovery is being set up.
  "send_email": [{ "name": "EMAIL" }],
  "analytics_engine_datasets": [
    { "binding": "USAGE", "dataset": "factlot_usage" },
  ],
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "run_worker_first": true,
    "not_found_handling": "404-page",
  },
  // Query strings are left out of logs and traces: /billing/success carries a checkout session id.
  // Known gap: Workers Logs has no option to redact URL paths (checked against the Cloudflare
  // docs, 2026-11-10: only `redact_query_string`, `head_sampling_rate`, `invocation_logs` and
  // log destinations exist). Live tokens ride in paths and are therefore stored in invocation
  // logs: /account/recover/<token>, /v1/billing/claim/<token>, /authorize/email/<link>,
  // /v1/reports/<token>... They are one-time or short-lived and the logs are owner-only, but the
  // exposure is real. Options, none applied here: set "invocation_logs": false inside "logs"
  // (drops request URLs, and with them the request log), or move the tokens to POST bodies or
  // URL fragments (a URL redesign).
  "observability": { "enabled": true, "redact_query_string": true },
}
